{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/348637-mummy-crossover-ideas","id":348637,"title":"Mummy Crossover Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-23T17:11:09-08:00","id":348637,"title":"Mummy Crossover Ideas","content":"So want to come up with a plot pitting my players against the Amenti...they consist of a Fenrir, Strider, Shadow Lord, CoG, and a Nuwisha...any plot ideas that would put a crowd like that at odds with the goals of an Amenti? I don't want a misunderstanding so much as have their goals interfere, issue is I've got some writers block. Yes I know combat wise a mummy won't do too well, but for me that's not so much the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T19:17:25-08:00","id":348695,"title":"","content":"Initial background questions. What ranks are the characters? and does the Strider have any Pure Breed? What is the packs totem, and does the pack have a goal they're set on long term?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T20:58:50-08:00","id":348774,"title":"","content":"The Strider is a rank 2 metis with the defect that he takes double agg from silver, and has a purebreed of 3, galliard. The Fenrir is a rank 4 ragabash, the Shadow Lord is a Rank 3 Philodox with the CoG being a Rank 2 CoG. The pack follows Crocodile, and then the Nuwisha is rank 4. The Strider does have a gaffling Ibis that follows him around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T00:00:37-08:00","id":348866,"title":"","content":"The Mummy needs the Strider's blood to complete a ritual to break a curse. The Strider's ancestor participated in cursing said mummy in ages past. Knowing Garou, they won't give their blood willingly to be used in magic, so the Mummy sets out to hunt the pack. Even if they find out and sympathize, you can have the curse be something they don't want broken. perhaps he (the Mummy) needs to free a Bane or Spectre to force information out of it.<br /> <br /> The Pack could, in the course of doing something else, mess up the Mummy's long term plans and he wants to make them pay for it, just out of spite. Not all Ameti are paragons of virtue. If a friend of his gets killed or hurt, or a relic broken, that could be enough motivation.<br /> <br /> Any chance the Mummy is a Bane Mummy? because that makes their goals clash much easier. Normal Ameti are actually quite Gaian in outlook, so making them have opposing goals is more work.<br /> <br /> It's late and the end of the work day, but more ideas will come. What is the setting of the Game? (year and place)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T09:04:48-08:00","id":349073,"title":"","content":"They're currently set in Western NY, but I can easily plop them in the Middle East if push really comes to shove. As for the Bane Mummy...yea I know I can use them, but I was just hoping to do a &quot;not evil&quot; antagonist. I you don't think its entirely possible, I can just switch out for the bane mummy. After a while of Fomor, Spirals, Banes, and Vamps....I wanted to toss a new threat their way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T23:57:30-08:00","id":349646,"title":"","content":"If using Revised Mummies, that is MtR versions, then remember that they have to be rather saintly to hold even a little magic to their name as Balance is both their power stat and extra strict version of Morality so if there is a conflict of interest with this kind of character it likely leaves the Garou on the immoral side of the divide as the bad guys more or less. Still the conflict could easily arrive from the fact that Garou tend to solve things by tooth and claw which the Mummy in question could find offensive to Ma'at and thus something that needed correcting, so this works if your Pack has had civilian casualties lately or just excessive use of force in general.<br /> <br /> If using Mummy 2nd edition then you have a much wider range of possibilities open to you as the Mummies in that system are much more free to act as they wish and pursue their own goals in addition to the larger goals. Then it can be anything ranging from a aforementioned need for blood or perhaps a fetish in possession of the PC's or a personal grudge with one of the PC's direct ancestors etc. They are also much less limited in their travels and so it wouldn't be that far stretched to find one of them visiting NY. The mummy may even see this conflict as unfortunate but necessary for some longer reaching goal to be fulfilled, perhaps he only need to distract the pack away from some other thing happening elsewhere that will advance it's long term goals even if not apparent in the short term. We are speaking of a being that is likely almost 4000 years old after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T19:27:40-08:00","id":350298,"title":"","content":"I only own stuff for the revised. I know they have to be saintly, but I wasn't quite sure if Ma'at jived entirely with the Garou and their view of Gaia. I figured I'd toss it up to the board to see if anyone had ideas on how to make a mummy tight with Ma'at still capable of being an antagonist. I was wondering if a Gaian view of morality could be used to put the two groups against each other where cultural relativism shows how both are in the &quot;right&quot; so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T03:27:33-08:00","id":350554,"title":"","content":"So as stated by Possessed above, if the pack has gotten any &quot;civilian&quot; casualties lately, an Ameti may well decide that they need punishment which would pit the mummy directly against the pack. Ameti generally come across as <i>more good</i> in comparison to Garou, according to western societal morality. So there is plenty for them to take issue with.<br /> I personally prefer to use the 2nd edition mummies, because as stated they are more open ended with what motivations can be. I used the revised book mostly for ideas/additional magics.<br /> I still like the idea of the Mummy having an issue with the Strider's ancestor. Moreso, since the Stiders don't get the ancestor background, so it would be much harder to find out why this creature is coming after him.<br /> As an added idea, if the mummy had a ritual that he needed werewolf components for, he could rationalize it away, as being perfectly ok to collect since the Garou are going to regenerate anyway. and that sort of thing will obviously not sit well with the players. just the idea of him magically tranqing a garou, and them waking later down a liver or ear or eye is kind of funny. As a ST, just make sure it doesn't battlescar, and let it heal once they shift forms. The damage to their pride and honor will be enough to send them hunting. With no lasting effects (the mummy could even have made sure it would heal) the Ameti could have his conscience free and clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T10:32:34-08:00","id":351792,"title":"","content":"Tomb Raidng Gone Bad!<br /> <br /> The Garou Pack heard claims of something -fetish, artifact, etc.- in a lost tomb in Egypt (or southern Sudan both are good). Problem is, there's a reason why the Tomb is lost and the Mummy(or mummies) guardian(s) will do everything to stop the Pack to get there and release what must remain Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 12-27-2014, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T12:29:52-08:00","id":352986,"title":"","content":"Definitely going to give these some thought. Thanks guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T11:43:28-07:00","id":1339031,"title":"","content":"It's very easy to use mummies as antagonists. You have to remember, and this is brought up in the Revised Silent Strider book, that mummies are **an affront to Gaia**. They're living beings who died and cheated death because of a foul ritual that fooled the Wyrm of Balance into allowing them to exist. This is a direct violation of Gaia's law, and nothing of Gaia can truly allow this to pass. They may have similar goals, but that doesn't matter. Mummies are violating the natural order, no matter how much lipservice they give to protecting it (and yes, I am a huge fan of Mummy; it's My favourite game).<br /> <br /> This is easiest for your SIlent Strider, because the Silent Striders put the Undying in the top 4 of their Tribal enemies. Above them are vampires, mages, and banes, and they really only plan to destroy the immortals after those enemies are out of the way (meaning that, as a tribe, no time soon), especially since the Undying cause the least amount of harm. It doesn't mean that a particularly zealous Silent Strider couldn't say, &quot;Fuck it. These abominations need to go!&quot; They shouldn't like that they're basically pissing all over Egypt, while the Silent Striders, Egypt's TRUE protectors, can't stay for any real length of time! <br /> <br /> Fenrir aren't going to like ANYTHING that comes back to life which hasn't expressly been given permission by Gaia, so mummies get no leeway. Add that the Fenrir HATE Necromancers, and most of the Undying are also necromancers, and there's plenty of reasons there. Nuwisha aren't like the Garou, but Nuwisha are still Gaian. Your Nuwisha might want to make the Mummies recognise how they defy the natural order that they serve and get them to destroy themselves, and in the most humourous way possible.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Lord is Garou, so we can point up to prior parts of this post for his or her motivation. The difference is that the Shadow Lord might want to first milk the mummies for as much information as they can find, which might help them to find out about these cults of blasphemers that keep bringing the dead back to life, so that they can destroy them and end the creation of more mummies once and for all. Even the Child of Gaia should be somewhat bloodthirsty in this, because these aren't innocent people. They're mummies and cults that make dead people into immortal people. You literally have the perfect party to do some hardcore mummy hunting. That they won't be able to keep them permanently dead means that you'll have a lot of good, long-term enemies. If they destroy the Resurrection Cults, that will make them VERY hostile enemies, to boot, while also giving the Garou massive amounts of Renown for permanently putting an end to the violation of Gaia's law through the creation of more of these unholy creatures. <br /> <br /> This is very simple and has lots of room for continued and sporadic use (only the dumbest of mummies are going to keep *directly* messing with a pack of Garou and Fera that want them dead).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T11:47:28-07:00","id":1339033,"title":"","content":"Aw, shit! This thread came up on a search that I was doing that involved mummies. I didn't see the *date* of the thread until after I replied to it, or I wouldn't have wasted time. Oh well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T17:35:13-07:00","id":1339730,"title":"","content":"Actually, the revised TB Silent Strider doesn't read that drastic to me. There is this:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Undying</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">During our first battles against the Cult of Sutekh,</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> a group of human wizards stumbled on the secrets of </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">immortality. And I mean real immortality, not this</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u201c</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">not dead but not alive</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u201d</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> shit you sometimes see. Their</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> leader claimed to be Horus, the son of Osiris, and as</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> such declared an eternal bloodfeud against Sutekh and</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> his Cult for killing his dad. And so these immortals </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">have spent thousands of years waging war against the</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> undead. Obviously, we decided it was in our best </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">interest to make friends with these guys. Well, friends </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">is really too strong of a word. Acquaintances, really.</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">We know they exist and they</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u2019</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">re generally aware of </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">what we are. Because our immediate interests inter-</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">sect, we work together on occasion. Note the </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u201c</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">on</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> occasion.</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u201d</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Not </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u201c</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">all the time.</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u201d</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> For one, there are not</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">many of them. And when something happens that</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> would kill them, it takes a while for them to come back </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">to life. So they aren</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u2019</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">t the most reliable of allies.</span></span><br /> <br /> There is another section, about the &quot;young immortals&quot; after the Sixth Mealstorm, and how they are mightier and more clueless... But still no enmity there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}